IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`
IMPORT `cdba-calendar`

-- Canada Disability Benefit Regulations (SOR/2025-35), section 1 -- DEFINITIONS.
--
-- The definitions that decide something are rules below. The others are names, and
-- they are glossed here rather than encoded:
--   "Act" means the Canada Disability Benefit Act.
--   "allocation" means the benefit portion that consists of the payments that are to
--      be made to a beneficiary as calculated in accordance with section 6: wherever
--      these modules say "allocation payment", they mean a payment so calculated.
--   "benefit" means a Canada disability benefit payable under the Act.
--   "supplemental amount" means the benefit portion the amount of which is set out in
--      section 6.1 (encoded there).
--   "cohabiting spouse or common-law partner" has the same meaning as in section 122.6
--      of the Income Tax Act, and "DTC-eligible individual" the meaning in subsection
--      146.4(1) of that Act. Neither Act is among the inputs, so each is a BORROWED
--      TERM: it is asked as a fact (a BOOLEAN field of `Person facts for a month`).

§ `Regulations s 1 -- Definitions`

-- src:20 | applicant means a person who has applied for a benefit or on whose behalf an application for a benefit has been made. (demandeur)
@ref Regulations s 1 "applicant" (src:20)
GIVEN `has applied for a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application for a benefit has been made on their behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is an applicant` `has applied for a benefit` `an application for a benefit has been made on their behalf` MEANS
        `has applied for a benefit`
     OR `an application for a benefit has been made on their behalf`

-- src:21 | beneficiary means a person to whom payment of a benefit has been approved or on whose behalf a benefit has become payable. (prestataire)
@ref Regulations s 1 "beneficiary" (src:21)
GIVEN `payment of a benefit has been approved to them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit has become payable on their behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a beneficiary` `payment of a benefit has been approved to them` `a benefit has become payable on their behalf` MEANS
        `payment of a benefit has been approved to them`
     OR `a benefit has become payable on their behalf`

-- "Payment period" means the period beginning on July 1 of a calendar year and ending
-- on June 30 of the following calendar year. A day belongs to the period that began on
-- the July 1 on or before it.
-- src:25 | payment period means the period beginning on July 1 of a calendar year and ending on June 30 of the following calendar year. (période de paiement)
@ref Regulations s 1 "payment period" (src:25)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the calendar year in which the payment period that includes the day begins` d MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH d AT LEAST 7
    THEN DATE_YEAR d
    ELSE DATE_YEAR d MINUS 1

@ref Regulations s 1 "payment period" (src:25)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Payment period`
`the payment period that includes the day` d MEANS
    `Payment period` WITH
        `the first day of the payment period` IS YearMonthDay (`the calendar year in which the payment period that includes the day begins` d) 7 1
        `the last day of the payment period`  IS YearMonthDay (`the calendar year in which the payment period that includes the day begins` d PLUS 1) 6 30

-- "the last taxation year that ended before the beginning of the payment period" is
-- used by s 2(1)(e), s 2(4) and s 6. ASSUMPTION (fork F8): a taxation year of an
-- individual is the calendar year. The Income Tax Act is not among the inputs, so the
-- Regulations do not say this; it is stated here once and nowhere else.
-- src:41 | (e) they have filed a return of income under the Income Tax Act for the last taxation year that ended before the beginning of the payment period in which that month falls.
@ref Regulations s 1 "payment period" (src:25); s 2(1)(e) (src:41)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the calendar year taken to be the last taxation year that ended before the payment period that includes the day began` d MEANS
    `the calendar year in which the payment period that includes the day begins` d MINUS 1

-- "Release", in relation to a person who has been incarcerated, means release from
-- custody on earned remission, at the expiry of a sentence, or on parole or statutory
-- release that has not been terminated or revoked.
-- src:26 | release, in relation to a person who has been incarcerated, means release from custody on earned remission, at the expiry of a sentence, or on parole or statutory release that has not been terminated or revoked. (libération)
@ref Regulations s 1 "release" (src:26)
GIVEN r IS A `Release event`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the event is a release` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `the way of the release`
    WHEN `release on earned remission`               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `release at the expiry of the sentence`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `release on parole`                         THEN NOT r's `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked`
    WHEN `release on statutory release`              THEN NOT r's `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked`
